module

public import Mathlib.RingTheory.EssentialFiniteness
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.LocalRing.RingHom.Basic
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.RingHom.Flat
public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.IsRegularScheme
import Mathlib.Algebra.MvPolynomial.Eval
import Mathlib.RingTheory.FiniteType
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Localization.Ideal
import Mathlib.RingTheory.RegularLocalRing.Polynomial

/-!
# Compatible regular local presentations over a field

Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Tags 00QM and 00OQ; the simultaneous polynomial-local
construction recorded in the DAG
(blueprint: lem-sfb-compatible-regular-local-field-presentations).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u v w

namespace Algebra

/-- A local map of local algebras essentially of finite type over a field admits
compatible surjections from regular local algebras essentially of finite type,
with flat local connecting map and regular local closed fibre essentially of finite type.
No flatness of the given map, completeness, or residue-field separability is required.

Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Tags 00QM (essentially finite type),
00F3 (finite type), 00OQ (polynomial regularity), 00CT (localization of a quotient),
00HT (flat localization), and 00HC (flat composition); simultaneous polynomial-local
construction (blueprint: lem-sfb-compatible-regular-local-field-presentations).

Proof:
1. By def-weil-pbc-essentially-finite-type-algebra and def-weil-pbc-finite-type-algebra,
   write `A = W⁻¹C` with `C` generated by finitely many elements over `k`.
   Evaluate `P = k[X₁,...,Xₙ]` in `A` at these generators, obtaining `a : P → A`.
   Each element of `A` is `a(h)/a(t)` with `a(t)` a unit. Set `p = a⁻¹(m_A)`
   and `R = P_p`. The fraction formula `q(h/t) = a(h)/a(t)` defines a surjection,
   and its maximal-ideal preimage is `pR = m_R`, so it is local.
   This uses def-weil-pbc-mv-polynomial-ring and def-weil-pbc-localization-at-prime.
2. Choose finite type generators presenting `B` as a localization similarly.
   Define `b : D = P[Y₁,...,Yₘ] → B` by `b(Xᵢ) = f(a(Xᵢ))` and the chosen
   images of `Yⱼ`. With `Q = b⁻¹(m_B)` and `S = D_Q`, fraction evaluation gives
   a surjective local map `v : S → B`; the `Y` variables alone give surjectivity.
3. Locality of `f` gives `f⁻¹(m_B) = m_A`, since units map to units. Thus
   `Q ∩ P = p`. Inclusion of polynomials induces the local map `u : R → S`.
   Both `v u` and `f q` send `h/t` to `f(a(h))/f(a(t))`. All three maps fix `k`.
4. By lem-weil-pbc-polynomial-ring-field-regular-ring, `R` and `S` are regular
   local. They are localizations of finite polynomial algebras, hence essentially
   of finite type by def-weil-pbc-essentially-finite-type-algebra.
5. Set `E = R[Y₁,...,Yₘ]`. Clearing the finitely many coefficient denominators
   identifies it with the localization of `D` at `P ∖ p`. These denominators avoid
   `Q`. If `Q_E` is the contraction of `QS` to `E`, the maps on fractions identify
   `S` with `E_{Q_E}` (def-weil-pbc-localization-at-prime).
6. Monomials give a free `R`-basis of `E` (def-weil-pbc-mv-polynomial-ring), so
   `R → E` is flat by lem-weil-pbc-projective-module-flat. Localization `E → S`
   is flat by lem-weil-pbc-localization-flat. Therefore `u` is flat by
   lem-weil-pbc-flat-ring-map-comp.
7. Put `K = R/m_R`, a field. Coefficient reduction identifies `E/m_R E` with
   `K[Y]`. Locality puts `m_R E` inside `Q_E`. By
   lem-weil-pbc-localization-at-prime-of-quotient, `S/m_R S` is the localization
   of `K[Y]` at the induced prime. It is regular local by
   lem-weil-pbc-polynomial-ring-field-regular-ring, with no separability condition.
8. Also `m_R S = pS`, and lem-weil-pbc-localization-at-prime-of-quotient identifies
   this same fibre with `(D/pD)_{Q/pD}`. The quotient `D/pD` is finite type over
   `k` on the images of the finitely many variables. Its localization is essentially
   of finite type over `k`. No finite type assertion about the field `K/k` is needed.
-/
theorem exists_compatible_regular_local_field_presentations
    (k : Type u) [Field k]
    (A : Type v) [CommRing A] [Algebra k A] [IsLocalRing A] [EssFiniteType k A]
    (B : Type w) [CommRing B] [Algebra k B] [IsLocalRing B] [EssFiniteType k B]
    (f : A →ₐ[k] B) [IsLocalHom f.toRingHom] :
    ∃ (R S : Type (max u v w)) (_ : CommRing R) (_ : CommRing S)
      (_ : Algebra k R) (_ : Algebra k S)
      (_ : IsRegularLocalRing R) (_ : IsRegularLocalRing S),
      EssFiniteType k R ∧ EssFiniteType k S ∧
        ∃ (q : R →ₐ[k] A) (v : S →ₐ[k] B) (u : R →ₐ[k] S),
          Function.Surjective q ∧ IsLocalHom q.toRingHom ∧
          Function.Surjective v ∧ IsLocalHom v.toRingHom ∧
          u.toRingHom.Flat ∧ IsLocalHom u.toRingHom ∧
          v.comp u = f.comp q ∧
          IsRegularLocalRing (S ⧸ (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R).map u.toRingHom) ∧
          EssFiniteType k (S ⧸ (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R).map u.toRingHom) := by
  sorry

end Algebra
